+## Seam analysis
+
+- Threads seat view, daemon handler, tier-3 test. These form one defect that crosses three clusters:
+  - `LazyMap::inspect` (src/daemon/compose.rs:1108-1119) sets `seat_view_error` only on `Rejected`/`Unsupported`. It leaves the slot unchanged on `Disconnected`, transport and discovery errors, including a `self.map().await?` failure.
+  - `roster_live::handle` (src/daemon/roster_live.rs:64-82) decides threads availability from that slot alone.
+  - Result: with herdr-threads down, `roster --live` reports `live_unavailable: null` and empty refusals and lost lists. If threads went down after an earlier good read, it reports the stale refusals from that read.
+  - tests/inspect_live.rs runs with no threads service and asserts exactly that output.
+  - Fixing the daemon alone turns the tier-3 test red, and fixing the test alone makes it fail against the current daemon. The two have to land together. Cluster 3 and cluster 10 each saw one half.
+- Integrity exit codes differ between the two roster modes:
+  - Daemon-free roster maps `InstructionError::Store(Integrity)` from Scope::resolve to exit 6 through `inspect::fail`.
+  - roster_live maps every Scope::resolve error to `bad_request`, exit 1 (src/daemon/roster_live.rs:50-51).
+  - The same input therefore exits differently depending on `--live`. Low reach, and cluster 3 already filed it as deferred.
+- One-HEAD rule for `ops --seat/--teamspace`:
+  - The CLI resolves names at its own pinned HEAD (src/cli/ops.rs:164), and the envelope carries the daemon's reply head.
+  - A commit landing between the two gives the invocation two HEADs. Both read the same repository and ids do not change, so the output is still right. Only the §2.1 statement is loose.
+- Roster `last_change` running inside the daemon:
+  - `roster.live` runs the full `build_inner`, including the HistoryWalker `last_change` pass, on the `GitStore` it shares with the writer (compose.rs `git = Arc::new(GitStore::open…)`, passed to both WriterCore and RosterLiveDeps).
+  - `HistoryWalker::commits` holds the repo mutex through a `Sort::TOPOLOGICAL` revwalk. Cluster 8 judged that plausibly O(full history). Per-commit diffs and `paths_at` reads then take the lock again for each commit.
+  - So a `roster --live` on a long history delays writer commits for that time. It does not break correctness, because the work runs in spawn_blocking and the lock is released between commits.
+- Malformed historical records:
+  - Cluster 5 found that an unparseable record in a historical tree aborts roster's `last_change` pass.
+  - Through the daemon, the same StoreError becomes a failed `roster.live` (`CommandError::from_store`). One bad historical record therefore blanks both roster modes, not just the daemon-free one.
+- Stale stub test against merged commands:
+  - `cli::tests::inspect_stubs_not_implemented` (src/cli/mod.rs:219-226) still runs `sessions` and calls `unwrap_err()`.
+  - `sessions` comes from another merged task (hg-blw.3) and returns Ok, so `cargo test --lib` is red at head. Only the composed branch shows this.
+  - The fix exists only on unmerged task-hg-blw.2 (9bf2777).
+- ops text mode against an older daemon: `ops` text mode now needs `head` in the `ops.list` reply, and IPC_VERSION was not bumped. Cluster 2 recorded this as deferred.
