+## Deferred OK
+- src/daemon/roster_live.rs:50-51: map `InstructionError::Store` through `CommandError::from_store` so an integrity failure during scope resolution exits 6 under `--live`, as it does daemon-free.
+- src/daemon/roster_live.rs:36-41: non-string scope words are dropped silently instead of being rejected as a bad request; only a malformed client sends them.
+- `ops --seat/--teamspace` resolves names at the CLI's HEAD while the envelope carries the daemon's reply head, so one invocation can see two HEADs; ids are stable, so the output is correct, but spec §2.1's one-HEAD wording should note the exception.
+- `ops` text mode requires `head` in the `ops.list` reply without an IPC_VERSION bump, so a pre-upgrade daemon still running makes plain `ops` fail with exit 1.
+- `ops --seat/--teamspace` resolves names before the daemon call, so with the daemon down it exits 1 or 2 instead of 5 (documented in tests/daemon_free_reads.rs).
+- `log` writes malformed-record warnings to stderr in text mode too, following the task 4 acceptance; spec §2.1's two statements on text-mode notices should be made consistent.
+- `roster.live` runs the HistoryWalker `last_change` pass on the GitStore shared with the writer, and `Sort::TOPOLOGICAL` in `HistoryWalker::commits` holds the repo mutex through what may be an O(full history) revwalk; drop the sort or measure it (performance only, output correct).
+- `last_touches` early exit compares distinct found paths against the input length, so duplicate inputs scan to the cap; dedupe when the stack consumer lands.
+- `paths_at` parses every teamspace and seat record for each scanned commit, and roster repeats it for each pending seat; the cost multiplier is understated for roster.
+- A malformed historical record aborts roster `last_change` and `log seat|teamspace` rather than degrading only the affected seat (spec §2.1 "one bad object never blanks a view"); the same applies through `roster.live`.
+- Spec §2.2 JSON shape omits `note`, `occupant.transcript`, the per-clone `live` overlay shape, the `seat_refusals`/`seat_lost` location and `unmanaged` placement, and §2.3 omits `stdin_payload`; sync the spec with the code when hg-blw.12 lands.
